{
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposal would be unacceptable principle as the property is not an appropriate size to be considered suitable for conversion, would fail to provide a family sized dwelling on the ground floor, and would not have regard to external space standards, contrary Local Plan policy SC6.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed extensions by reason of their excessive size and scale would fail to reflect to the proportions of the host dwelling and would not appear subordinate. The proposed hip to gable roof conversion would fail to respect the character of the original house and would unbalance the pair of semi-detached properties. The proposal would harm the character and appearance of the host property and wider area, contrary to Local Plan policies CC1, CC2, and SC7 and the intent of Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD. ",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed single storey rear extensions would result in an increased sense of enclosure, overbearingness, and a loss of outlook that would harm the living conditions of the adjoining neighbour. The proposed development would therefore be contrary to Local Plan Policies CC2 and SC7 and the intent of Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD.",
    "Reason : 4 - The proposed development, due to the cramped and poor of layout of the studio unit and lack of private amenity space for the three bedroom unit, would result in substandard living conditions. The proposed development is therefore contrary to London Plan policy D6 and Local Plan policies SC5 and SC6. ",
    "Reason : 5 - The application has failed to demonstrate that the proposal would not result in harm to highway and pedestrian safety and additional excessive parking stress on the roads surrounding the development. The proposed development is therefore contrary to Local Plan policy EC2 and the Residential Crossovers and Off-Street Parking Policy."
  ],
